<title>SINGAPORE: Hai Sun Hup net up 21 pct to S$36.79 mln.</title>
<headline>Hai Sun Hup net up 21 pct to S$36.79 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		36.79     vs     30.41</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)	  10.00     vs     10.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	8.50     vs	7.70</p>
<p>    Turnover		 389.18     vs    343.04</p>
<p>    Investment income	0.23     vs	nil</p>
<p>    Other income	    17.26     vs     13.11</p>
<p>    Interest expense	22.20     vs     17.54</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    25.56     vs     23.77</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	  35.90     vs     28.66</p>
<p>    Associates		 5.26     vs	6.37</p>
<p>    Tax			  3.79     vs	4.16</p>
<p>    Minorities	(loss) 0.58     vs	0.46 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (loss) 3.51     vs	nil</p>
<p>Dividend pay date - September 17 1997  </p>
<p>Last date books open - September 4 1997</p>
<p>Note - Shipping-based Hai Sun Hup Group Ltd said the extraordinary items comprised a S$1.71 million loss from the disposal of an investment in Hub International Container Line Pte Ltd, the group's share of the net liabilities of Hub and a S$1.8 million loss in the disposal of the 20-year-old supertanker &quot;Sentosa Pride&quot;.</p>
</text>
